    # log T's block size from an upper bound on its encoding: the extents ALREADY recorded (the dataset phase's ALLOCs
    # and FREEs — a truncation's kills among them, which belong to no dirty block: B5 review) plus, for each MOS block
    # still to finalise (log T's own included), <= 3 DVAs allocated and <= 3 freed — never more than the list holds
    # (ZWK_MAXXL); a two-word entry each; a debug word per metaslab and type; a pad word per block boundary — the
    # smallest power of two >= that and the allocation unit. ZWK_MAXXL bounds it at 8 x (2 x 4,096 + 2 x 2,048 + 1)
